    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0568" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.51/11–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Praha</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-05T17:00:00+02:00">November 5, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 6—7:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>529. The Deputy Chief of the Economic Section of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
                    has informed the Embassy in the strictest confidence that the Zecho authorities
                    intend to avail themselves of not more than 20 million dollars of the proposed
                    Export-Import Bank cotton credit as arrangements have been made with the Soviet
                    Govt to procure the balance of their cotton requirements from the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
